      "name": "library-ingestion",
      "title": "Library ingestion — the basic flow",
      "description": "The BASIC ingestion flow every asset takes: an upload is accepted, its metadata goes into the knowledge graph, and the asset lands in `library/<slug>/` if it is materialized. The two entry points (a drop in `uploads/`, or materializing an asset a remote graph lists), what happens to the upload afterwards, and why content-type methods refine this flow from above rather than living in it. Command: `bun run cat ingest`.",
